#: Game.Levels.DFA.L11_Language
msgid "**Final level of this world.**\n"
"\n"
"§0 accepts exactly the strings with an even number of §1s.\n"
"\n"
"Everything you need is already in your inventory: §2, §3,\n"
"§4, §5, §6 and §7. In one case you will need\n"
"to show a state is *not* accepting: remember the pattern from the\n"
"counterexample level, §8.\n"
"\n"
"One new tactic: §9 changes any goal into §10. From a contradiction\n"
"you can prove anything, so when your assumptions contradict each other, use\n"
"§11 and then derive §12."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rw [h]`
#. §1: `h : X = Y`
#. §2: `h : X ↔ Y`
#. §3: `X`
#. §4: `Y`
#. §5: `rw [h₁, h₂]`
#. §6: `rw [← h]`
#. §7: `rw [h] at h'`
#. §8: `h'`
#. §9: `rw`
#: Game.Doc.Tactics
msgid "§0, where §1 (or §2), replaces §3 by §4 in the goal.\n"
"\n"
"* §5 rewrites with several facts in turn.\n"
"* §6 rewrites right-to-left.\n"
"* §7 rewrites in the assumption §8 instead of the goal.\n"
"\n"
"After rewriting, §9 tries to close the goal if both sides became identical."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `by_cases h : «{n}» % 2 = 0`
